Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
Electron's refactor_expose_file_system_access_blocklist.patch relocates
NormalizeFilePath() and GenerateBlockPaths() from this .cc into static
members of ChromeFileSystemAccessPermissionContext in the header (Electron
does not compile the .cc), so the new MaybeStripMacDataVolumePrefix() and
NormalizeFilePathForBlocklist() helpers and the /System/Volumes
kBlockAllChildren rule are added to that header copy instead, and the .cc's
ShouldBlockAccessToPath() calls the header's static helper. The
chrome/browser unittest hunk is dropped (not built by Electron). Electron's
own ShouldBlockAccessToPath() in
shell/browser/file_system_access/file_system_access_permission_context.cc
is switched to NormalizeFilePathForBlocklist() in a companion Electron
commit.

